# d7_weight_init_free
# basis      d6 peak 683016 kB; Tensor2D<unsigned long>::Tensor2D 647012 kB (96.5% attributed,
#            97.7% of the peak), the only sizable object at that instant.
# phase      d6 moved the peak from the end-of-run key ramp to a startup transient (t=0.5 s, ~21 ms):
#            net.init() randomising all twelve FC weights. Hence d6 -1.4% and the earlier campaign's
#            d7 (missing `delete[] squares`) +0.04%.
# existing   lazy-weight lever (before d6): llama_base.h skips up-front masking of large FC weights,
#            records maskCtr, frees; FC::_forward re-materialises via ensureData(), restores the
#            counter, masks, frees. Masks and keys byte-identical.
# lever      free each weight at the end of its own _initScale: one layer resident instead of twelve.
#            Randomisation unchanged (seed, values, order); shape kept (d1/d2 separate from data);
#            restore path = the ensureData() path gating since d5.
# expected   weight term 647 MB -> one layer's largest FC weight (768 x 3072 x 8 B = 18.9 MB); peak
#            then bounded by the ~500 MB end-of-run allocator floor.
# impl_snapshot: overlay.patch
# Only step of this line with its source overlay in the repository (this directory).
# pool_attacked: host
# object_attacked: Tensor2D<unsigned long>::Tensor2D
OMP_NUM_THREADS=16
MALLOC_ARENA_MAX=2
